# reviews-insight API, the REST surface (Day 5).
#
# How to use:
#   1. Start the server:  poetry run reviews serve
#   2. Open this file in an editor with a REST client (VS Code "REST Client"
#      extension, or the JetBrains HTTP Client) and click "Send Request" above
#      each request. Each block is separated by a line of three hashes.
#
# Base URL. Change the port here if you started the server with --port.
@host = http://127.0.0.1:8000
@contentType = application/json

### Health: the liveness route returns {"status":"ok"}.
GET {{host}}/health

### Create a review: a valid body is accepted with 201 and a ReviewAccepted response.
POST {{host}}/v1/reviews
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"product_id": "P1", "rating": 5}

### Rejected at the edge: a rating of 11 is outside 1 to 5, so pydantic returns 422.
POST {{host}}/v1/reviews
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"product_id": "P1", "rating": 11}

### Rejected at the edge: an empty product_id fails the min_length rule, also 422.
POST {{host}}/v1/reviews
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"product_id": "", "rating": 5}

### Add a few more so the list has something to page over.
POST {{host}}/v1/reviews
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"product_id": "P2", "rating": 4}

###
POST {{host}}/v1/reviews
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"product_id": "P3", "rating": 3}

### Pagination: ask for one page (limit 2, starting at offset 0). The response
### carries items plus total, limit, and offset, never the whole collection.
GET {{host}}/v1/reviews?limit=2&offset=0

### The next page: same limit, offset moved forward by 2.
GET {{host}}/v1/reviews?limit=2&offset=2

### Insight: the summary over everything submitted so far.
GET {{host}}/v1/insight

### The machine-readable contract. The versioned route /v1/reviews is listed in it.
GET {{host}}/openapi.json
